-- TrainOS fixture world, part 2 — Enquiries, TNAs, proposals, quotations and the client portal
--
-- Tenant: akademi-perdana (Akademi Perdana Sdn Bhd), id acade111-0000-4000-8000-000000000001
--
-- Run (all four parts, one transaction, from the repo root):
--   psql "$DATABASE_URL" -1 -v ON_ERROR_STOP=1 \
--     -f supabase/seeds/fixture_world_01_tenant_and_parties.sql \
--     -f supabase/seeds/fixture_world_02_sales_and_money.sql \
--     -f supabase/seeds/fixture_world_03_delivery_compliance_finance.sql \
--     -f supabase/seeds/fixture_world_04_ai_ops_and_agents.sql
--
-- Targets migrations 001-017: the tenant is provisioned by
-- app.provision_tenant() from 016, so this does NOT run against a database at
-- 013 or earlier. 018 adds RPCs, not configuration this seed writes — the
-- pipeline rows below are the seed's own, and no provisioning pack writes
-- stages yet.
--
-- Idempotent: every statement is an upsert guarded by an IS DISTINCT FROM
-- comparison, so a second run of an unchanged seed performs zero updates and
-- leaves every updated_at where it was. Iterating a fixture never needs a wipe,
-- with two exceptions named in supabase/seeds/README.md.
--
-- One of the four parts of the TrainOS fixture world. The parts are in
-- foreign-key order and must be run in order:
--
--   1. fixture_world_01_tenant_and_parties.sql
--   2. fixture_world_02_sales_and_money.sql
--   3. fixture_world_03_delivery_compliance_finance.sql
--   4. fixture_world_04_ai_ops_and_agents.sql
--
-- Companion files:
--   fixture_world_wipe.sql         removes every row the four parts write, tenant included
--   test_fixture_world.sql         the pin: counts, landmarks, re-run stability
--
-- Generated by packages/fixtures/scripts/emit-seed.ts — edit the fixtures or the
-- generator, never this file. Regenerate with:
--   npx tsx packages/fixtures/scripts/emit-seed.ts
-- and `--check` fails if the committed SQL and the fixtures have drifted apart.

-- Suspend the gates for this load; restored at the foot of this file.
